  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 935228c0fd2628c4db5028980babef0b, type: 3}
  m_Name: NarrativeParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.NarrativeParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: 'Let''s take a look at how local lights are set up.


      1. In the <i>Hierarchy,</i> expand one of the lamp prefabs in the corridor, for instance <b>Spotlight_Entrance_04.</b>


      2. Select the <b>Spot Light</b> GameObject in the prefab.


      3. Experiment with different <b>Inner / Outer Spot Angles,</b>  <b>Intensity</b> and <b>Range.</b>


      4. Undo your change.



      <b>Expert tips</b>


      To optimize performance, you may decide to reduce the number of real-time lights, turn their shadows off, or set their <b>Mode</b> to <b>Baked.</b>'
